# Oracle Integration Standards

## Pyth Feed Requirements
- Always read `price`, `conf`, `expo`, and `publish_time` from the feed account
- Reject stale data: `publish_time` must be within `MAX_STALENESS_SECONDS` (default: 60s)
- Reject low confidence: `conf / price` must be below `MAX_CONFIDENCE_RATIO` (default: 0.05)

## Trigger Evaluation
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — full validation before trigger
function evaluateTrigger(feed: PriceFeed, rule: TriggerRule): TriggerResult {
  if (isStale(feed.publishTime, MAX_STALENESS_SECONDS)) {
    return { triggered: false, reason: 'STALE_ORACLE' };
  }
  if (feed.conf / feed.price > MAX_CONFIDENCE_RATIO) {
    return { triggered: false, reason: 'LOW_CONFIDENCE' };
  }
  return { triggered: feed.price < rule.threshold, reason: 'EVALUATED' };
}
```

## MVP Constraint
- Single feed only — do not implement multi-oracle aggregation
- Document the chosen feed ID and network in `oracle-connector/README.md`

## Error Handling
- Log all rejected oracle reads with timestamp, feed ID, and rejection reason
- Never trigger payout on oracle read failure — fail closed
